whole grains, grain products, feed ingredients, domestic fuel products, and other agricultural commodities. The Renewables segment produces, purchases, sells, merchandises, and trades in ethanol, and co-products, as well as merchandises and trades in other biofuels, such as renewable feedstocks. The Andersons, Inc. was founded in 1947 and is based in Maumee, Ohio.","ceo_bio":"Mr. William E. Krueger | CEO, President & Director | Age 58 | Compensation: $2.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $5.4M ranks in the top quartile among Consumer Defensive peers, with revenue growing 8%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $8K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["The Andersons, Inc. is a small-cap consumer defensive business with a $1.5B market cap on $11.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -14% over the past three years and +114% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 7% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The company is burning through $56M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.9\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 3.1\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 2.8% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 4.1% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 189% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.8946457950958602},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Consumer Defensive peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.0% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Consumer Defensive peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Widening credit spreads suggest growing stress in corporate debt markets","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"GLP-1 and health-trend demand destruction \u2014 weight-loss drugs and wellness shifts are structurally reducing consumption in snack, beverage, and packaged food categories.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 24% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","29 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Consumer Defensive sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 15% over 3 months","Con