rage (3.0x equity multiplier).","It spends 0.2% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is moderate at 1.9x net debt to EBITDA ($98.3M of cash against $623.4M of debt), above the 1.5x gate, with interest covered 3.1x.","No distress or manipulation flags (Altman Z 4.1, in the safe zone)."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at -14.0% over 3 years and 6.0% over 5 years, so growth is decelerating.","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Capex runs 1.7x depreciation (2.1% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth.","Its Rule of 40 score is 5, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 4.1%, and institutions hold 95%.","It returns 2.8% a year to shareholders (1.0% in buybacks and 1.8% in dividends).","It has paid a dividend for 29 consecutive years, raising it 3.1% a year over the last five."],"people":["With about 2,028 employees, each generates about $5.4M of revenue, 10.6x the Consumer Defensive median, and revenue has grown 8.2% a year across its filed history.","Free cash flow is negative, at -$28K per employee.","CEO pay is $2.4M (0x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (1/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $8K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":43,"head":"Avoid: priced 189% above its fair value of $15.54.","pros":["Altman Z in the safe zone","P/E 7.6x vs sector 17.5x","EV/EBITDA 7.6x vs sector 10.0x","3 analysts' mean target $90.00 (+100%)","12-1 month momentum +36%"],"cons":["Trades 189% above fair value of $15.54","ROIC 7.8% vs WACC 7.9%","FCF margin 0.5% (burns cash)"],"flags":["Priced 189% above its fair value of $15.54","Earns below its cost of capital and burns cash"],"need":[],"buy_below":13.21,"vc":{"base":15.54,"base_src":"blend","bear":null,"bull":null,"alt_median":15.54,"n_alt":3,"gap":null,"dispersion":0.1113,"level":"MEDIUM","why":[]},"med":{"pe":1